From 55e10390d775a567eb6f0e73364eddc69f6fd687 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: shota <monyuonyu@gmail.com>
Date: Sun, 27 Sep 2026 14:40:08 +0900
Subject: [PATCH 106/106] Unified: error messages of features in the user's
 language

Many messages thrown by FreeCAD and OCC are not marked for translation
('Wire is not closed.', 'BRep_API: command not done', attacher and
pattern errors), and some carry numbers or names ('... conflicting
constraints: 5, 6', 'subshape not found Pad.Face9'). A translator
installed ahead of the others (Gui::Translator::addOverride takes a
QTranslator now) translates them in the error contexts: 'Exception',
'Notifications' and the object's type (the tree's tooltip). It uses the
module's own translation of the whole message first, then the
'UnifiedErrors' context: the message worded for the type of object (a
fillet that fails suggests a smaller radius), the message, patterns with
numbers or names, and a known beginning followed by a name. 290 messages
of PartDesign, Sketcher and Part are translated into Japanese.

The notification area looks the object up by the label in front of the
message to word it for its type; the design check does the same.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
